WEBVTT

00:00.070 --> 00:12.600
This is a showcase website I built for K&R Robak Remonty, a renovation company from Małopolska in Poland. What you see is a local copy, filled with sample content and generated placeholder photos.

00:14.110 --> 00:18.390
The site comes in Polish, German and English. Here is the German version.

00:19.890 --> 00:24.730
And English. A text missing in a language falls back to Polish, field by field.

00:26.230 --> 00:29.110
Visitors can switch between a light and a dark theme.

00:31.110 --> 00:36.580
The services section lists the six kinds of work the company does, and each one has its own page.

00:38.090 --> 00:42.600
Below are albums of finished jobs. Every album in this recording is a sample.

00:44.100 --> 00:46.560
Opening an album shows its photo viewer.

00:46.580 --> 00:49.180
Visitors can step through the photos with the arrows,

00:50.180 --> 00:52.380
jump to any photo from the thumbnails,

00:53.380 --> 00:55.210
or open one in full screen.

00:57.240 --> 01:04.180
Now the other side: the admin panel, which the owner uses alone. It is in Polish. This is the list of albums.

01:06.180 --> 01:08.160
Adding an album starts with a title.

01:11.600 --> 01:18.700
One click creates it. Photos are compressed to WebP in the browser before they are uploaded, which keeps the server within the free tier.

01:23.210 --> 01:28.510
An album with photos can be edited: captions, their order and which photo is the cover.

01:32.080 --> 01:36.620
A switch decides whether visitors can see the album. I will hide this one and save.

01:38.870 --> 01:45.640
The public list is already updated. There is no redeploy, because the pages read the database on every request.

01:48.140 --> 01:52.750
The general settings hold the language switches and the contact data shown on the site.

01:56.880 --> 02:04.020
The whole project runs on one Cloudflare Worker, with D1 for the data and R2 for the photos, at no running cost.
